# The step-cap and window sweep, its second screen, on the same sample of the agents (seed 11). The first screen showed
# the gateway's static cap lowering the change's share of replies over the SLO (41% without a cap, 32% at 8, 25% at 4)
# at the same agents' throughput, and a step cap of 256 lowering it to 15%, against 56% at 1,024. This one takes the cap
# to 2 and to 1, combines the 256-token step cap with caps of 4 and 2, gives tuned vLLM the same step cap and caps, and
# runs the change with the KV cache in FP8, which doubles the pool's tokens (the quality gate screens FP8's outputs).
# The FP8 points come last: an engine that does not start with them stops only them.
#   benchmarks/e2/campaign.sh --pause benchmarks/e2/sweep-screen2.campaign

agents-seed 11

# engine frozen
arms/sweep-disc-frozen-cap2-s24.toml
arms/sweep-disc-frozen-cap1-s24.toml

# engine frozen --max-num-batched-tokens 256 --long-prefill-token-threshold 0
arms/sweep-disc-frozen-b256-t0-s24.toml

# engine make-room (48-token window)
arms/sweep-disc-pr-ab48-cap2-s24.toml
arms/sweep-disc-pr-ab48-cap1-s24.toml

# engine make-room (48-token window) --max-num-batched-tokens 256 --long-prefill-token-threshold 0
arms/sweep-disc-pr-ab48-b256-cap4-s24.toml
arms/sweep-disc-pr-ab48-b256-cap2-s24.toml

# engine make-room (48-token window) --kv-cache-dtype fp8
arms/sweep-disc-pr-ab48-fp8-s24.toml

# engine make-room (48-token window) --max-num-batched-tokens 256 --long-prefill-token-threshold 0 --kv-cache-dtype fp8
arms/sweep-disc-pr-ab48-b256-fp8-s24.toml
